#: ../../source/journal.rst:202
msgid "Sémantique de ``Apply``"
msgstr "Semantics of ``Apply``"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:204
msgid ""
"``func (s *State) Apply(ev Event) error`` applique un événement. "
"**Première règle** : si ``ev.Kind != EvCreated`` et ``s.Current < 0``, "
"erreur « tournoi non créé ». Aucun événement ne peut précéder la "
"création."
msgstr ""
"``func (s *State) Apply(ev Event) error`` applies an event. **First "
"rule**: if ``ev.Kind != EvCreated`` and ``s.Current < 0``, error "
"\"tournament not created\". No event can precede creation."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:208
msgid ""
"Avant le traitement, ``s.clock = ev.Time``. Un ``Kind`` inconnu est une "
"erreur (« événement inconnu »)."
msgstr ""
"Before processing, ``s.clock = ev.Time``. An unknown ``Kind`` is an error"
" (\"unknown event\")."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:211
msgid ""
"À la fin de tout traitement réussi, et pour **tous** les types y compris "
"``note`` :"
msgstr ""
"At the end of any successful processing, and for **all** types including "
"``note``:"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:220
msgid ""
"``check()`` est rappelée sur ces trois types parce qu'ils changent ce "
"qu'elle regarde (les joueurs qui occupent une place de graphe, un score "
"au regard de la longueur, deux matchs sur une même table) sans passer par"
" ``recompute()``, qui l'appelle déjà. ``refreshInfos()`` recalcule "
"``State.Infos``."
msgstr ""
"``check()`` is called again on these three types because they change what"
" it looks at (the players occupying a graph slot, a score with respect to"
" the length, two matches on the same table) without going through "
"``recompute()``, which already calls it. ``refreshInfos()`` recomputes "
"``State.Infos``."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:225
msgid ""
"``NEvents`` est donc le nombre d'événements appliqués avec succès ; il "
"entre dans la graine du générateur, ce qui garantit qu'une nouvelle "
"proposition suit toujours un tirage différent."
msgstr ""
"``NEvents`` is therefore the number of events applied successfully; it "
"enters the generator's seed, which guarantees that a new proposal always "
"follows a different draw."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:239
msgid ""
"Un second ``created`` dans un journal écraserait la configuration ; le "
"moteur ne l'interdit pas explicitement, mais l'hôte ne doit jamais le "
"produire."
msgstr ""
"A second ``created`` in a journal would overwrite the configuration; the "
"engine does not explicitly forbid it, but the host must never produce "
"one."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:258
msgid "**Retardataires.** Trois chemins, et un seul interdit : refaire le tirage."
msgstr "**Latecomers.** Three paths, and only one is forbidden: redoing the draw."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:260
msgid ""
"Le tirage n'a pas eu lieu (ou la phase est un suisse non figé) : le "
"joueur entre tout de suite, avec toutes ses vies."
msgstr ""
"The draw has not taken place (or the phase is an unfrozen Swiss): the "
"player enters immediately, with all their lives."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:262
msgid ""
"``ev.Slot`` désigne une **place d'exemption libre** d'un tableau déjà "
"tiré (``State.FreeSlots`` les énumère, ``PlayerAddedAtSlotEvent`` "
"construit l'événement) : il l'occupe là où elle est, avec une vie — il ne"
" bénéficie pas de l'exemption qu'il prend. Une place dont le match a été "
"lancé, ou dont le tour a commencé, ou qui n'existe pas, est **refusée** :"
" ``Apply`` renvoie une erreur."
msgstr ""
"``ev.Slot`` designates a **free bye slot** in a bracket that has already "
"been drawn (``State.FreeSlots`` enumerates them, "
"``PlayerAddedAtSlotEvent`` builds the event): the player takes it where "
"it is, with one life — they do not benefit from the bye they take. A slot"
" whose match has been started, or whose round has begun, or which does "
"not exist, is **refused**: ``Apply`` returns an error."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:266
msgid ""
"Sinon il est enregistré (``Players``, ``Order``) sans entrer dans aucune "
"phase, et ``State.Infos`` porte un code disant où il entrera "
"(``enters_at``) ou que rien ne l'admet (``no_entry``)."
msgstr ""
"Otherwise the player is recorded (``Players``, ``Order``) without "
"entering any phase, and ``State.Infos`` carries a code saying where they "
"will enter (``enters_at``) or that nothing admits them (``no_entry``)."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:279
msgid ""
"La **correction d'une fiche** — nom, club, cote — et rien d'autre. La "
"fiche est entière, comme la configuration de ``config_changed`` : ce qui "
"est écrit est le résultat. L'état du joueur n'est pas touché : un retiré "
"reste retiré, ses vies, ses victoires, ses matchs et sa place dans les "
"phases sont intacts."
msgstr ""
"The **correction of a record** — name, club, rating — and nothing else. "
"The record is complete, like the configuration of ``config_changed``: "
"what is written is the result. The player's state is not touched: a "
"withdrawn player stays withdrawn, and their lives, wins, matches and "
"place in the phases are intact."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:284
msgid ""
"Ce n'est **pas une réinscription**, et c'est ce qui la distingue de "
"``player_added`` sur un identifiant connu, qui met la fiche à jour **et**"
" annule un retrait : corriger le club d'une joueuse retirée par "
"``player_added`` la remettrait en jeu. ``player_added`` garde son sens "
"pour les journaux existants — c'est aussi le chemin du retour d'un joueur"
" retiré."
msgstr ""
"This is **not a re-registration**, and that is what distinguishes it from"
" ``player_added`` on a known identifier, which updates the record **and**"
" cancels a withdrawal: correcting the club of a player withdrawn via "
"``player_added`` would put her back in play. ``player_added`` keeps its "
"meaning for existing journals — it is also the path for the return of a "
"withdrawn player."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:291
msgid "``player_unavailable`` et ``player_available``"
msgstr "``player_unavailable`` and ``player_available``"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:303
msgid ""
"Un joueur **indisponible** n'est plus apparié, et ne perd rien : ni vie, "
"ni victoire, ni rang, ni place dans un tableau. C'est le joueur qui ne "
"revient que dimanche à 14 h, celui qui dîne, celui qui joue en ce moment "
"dans une autre épreuve de la salle. Les autres moyens ne conviennent pas "
": le retirer puis le réinscrire le classe « forfait » pendant l'absence, "
"ne rien faire le laisse apparier, et un forfait lui coûte une vie."
msgstr ""
"An **unavailable** player is no longer paired, and loses nothing: no "
"life, no win, no rank, no place in a bracket. This is the player who only"
" returns on Sunday at 14h, the one who is having dinner, the one who is "
"currently playing in another event in the playing hall. The other options"
" do not fit: withdrawing then re-registering the player ranks them as a "
"\"forfeit\" during the absence, doing nothing leaves them to be paired, "
"and a forfeit costs them a life."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:317
msgid "L'absence tombe :"
msgstr "The absence ends:"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:319
msgid ""
"à l'heure ``Until`` (comparée à l'heure de la proposition, "
"``ProposeAt(now)``, ou de l'événement en cours d'application) ;"
msgstr ""
"at time ``Until`` (compared with the proposal time, ``ProposeAt(now)``, "
"or with the time of the event being applied);"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:321
msgid ""
"pour une absence « jusqu'à la ronde ``Round`` », quand la ronde appariée "
"atteint ``Round``, ou au passage à une autre phase ;"
msgstr ""
"for an absence \"until round ``Round``\", when the paired round reaches "
"``Round``, or on moving to another phase;"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:323
msgid ""
"sans échéance, à ``player_available``, qui lève aussi toute absence avant"
" son terme."
msgstr ""
"with no deadline, at ``player_available``, which also lifts any absence "
"before its end."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:325
msgid "Effets, tous dérivés :"
msgstr "Effects, all derived:"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:327
msgid ""
"**suisse** : ``free(ph, r)`` écarte les absents — en continu comme par "
"rondes (la ronde ``r`` est celle qu'on apparie). Un absent n'est pas dans"
" le ``Roster`` de la ronde : la ronde se termine sans lui, **sans bye**. "
"La file porte une attente par absent en vie (``wait``, raison "
"``player_unavailable``, ``A`` = le joueur, ``Until`` ou ``Round`` = son "
"retour) ;"
msgstr ""
"**Swiss**: ``free(ph, r)`` excludes the absent players — in continuous "
"mode as in rounds mode (round ``r`` is the one being paired). An absent "
"player is not in the round's ``Roster``: the round ends without them, "
"**without a bye**. The queue carries one wait per absent player who is "
"alive (``wait``, reason ``player_unavailable``, ``A`` = the player, "
"``Until`` or ``Round`` = their return);"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:331
msgid ""
"**graphes** (tableaux, GSL, poules, barrages) : la place est fixée, le "
"match d'un absent reste donc proposé, mais **retenu** — raison "
"``player_unavailable``, sans table. Le TD peut le lancer quand même."
msgstr ""
"**graphs** (brackets, GSL, pools, play-offs): the slot is fixed, so an "
"absent player's match is still proposed, but **held** — reason "
"``player_unavailable``, with no table. The TD can start it anyway."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:351
msgid ""
"Le retrait est **général** : le joueur quitte le tournoi. Ses matchs de "
"graphe non encore lancés sont perdus par walkover lors de la résolution "
"(voir :ref:`graphes`)."
msgstr ""
"Withdrawal is **general**: the player leaves the tournament. Their graph "
"matches not yet started are lost by walkover at resolution (see "
":ref:`graphes`)."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:354
msgid ""
"**Retrait différé** (``AfterCurrent``, "
"``PlayerWithdrawnAfterCurrentEvent``) : le joueur qui doit partir finit "
"le match qu'il joue. Il est inscrit dans ``WithdrawAfter`` ; occupé, il "
"n'est plus apparié ; ``promoteDeferred()``, appelée après chaque "
"résultat, le fait passer dans ``Withdrawn`` dès qu'il n'a plus de match "
"en cours. S'il n'a pas de match en cours, le retrait est immédiat."
msgstr ""
"**Deferred withdrawal** (``AfterCurrent``, "
"``PlayerWithdrawnAfterCurrentEvent``): the player who has to leave "
"finishes the match they are playing. They are recorded in "
"``WithdrawAfter``; while busy, they are no longer paired; "
"``promoteDeferred()``, called after each result, moves them into "
"``Withdrawn`` as soon as they have no match in progress. If they have no "
"match in progress, the withdrawal is immediate."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:359
msgid ""
"Le **forfait d'un seul match**, sans quitter le tournoi, n'est pas un "
"retrait : c'est un ``result`` avec ``Forfeit = true`` (``ForfeitEvent``),"
" après lequel le perdant suit le chemin d'un perdant ordinaire."
msgstr ""
"A **single-match forfeit**, without leaving the tournament, is not a "
"withdrawal: it is a ``result`` with ``Forfeit = true`` "
"(``ForfeitEvent``), after which the loser follows the path of an ordinary"
" loser."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:363
msgid ""
"Un qualifié de poule qui se retire avant le tirage de la phase suivante "
"ouvre un repêchage (proposé, voir :ref:`format_poules`)."
msgstr ""
"A pool qualifier who withdraws before the draw of the next phase opens a "
"repechage (proposed, see :ref:`format_poules`)."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:369
msgid "Validations, dans l'ordre :"
msgstr "Validations, in order:"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:379
msgid ""
"``busy(p)`` : il existe un match de statut ``Running`` où ``p`` joue. "
"**Un joueur ne peut jamais avoir deux matchs en cours.** C'est "
"l'invariant central de l'ordonnancement."
msgstr ""
"``busy(p)``: there is a match with status ``Running`` in which ``p`` "
"plays. **A player can never have two matches in progress.** This is the "
"central invariant of scheduling."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:382
msgid "Puis :"
msgstr "Then:"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:400
#, no-python-format
msgid ""
"``ev.Round`` (relu du libellé ``\"Ronde %d\"`` pour un journal de version"
" 0, voir ``Event.upgraded``) est le seul mécanisme qui fait avancer le "
"compteur de rondes du suisse synchrone. ``openRound`` n'agit que dans un "
"``swiss_lives`` en mode ``rounds`` et pour ``ev.Round > ph.Round`` : au "
"premier événement d'une ronde (match ou bye) et avant de l'appliquer, il "
"relève les joueurs libres de la phase (``free(ph, r)``) ; ce sont les "
"joueurs appelés à la ronde (voir :ref:`format_suisse`)."
msgstr ""
"``ev.Round`` (re-read from the label ``\"Ronde %d\"`` for a version 0 "
"journal, see ``Event.upgraded``) is the only mechanism that advances the "
"round counter of the synchronous Swiss. ``openRound`` acts only in a "
"``swiss_lives`` in ``rounds`` mode and for ``ev.Round > ph.Round``: at "
"the first event of a round (match or bye), and before applying it, it "
"collects the free players of the phase (``free(ph, r)``); these are the "
"players called to the round (see :ref:`format_suisse`)."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:406
msgid ""
"``nextMatchID()`` renvoie ``\"M\" + (nextID+1)``. Comme ``nextID`` n'est "
"incrémenté que par ``match_started``, les identifiants sont consécutifs à"
" partir de ``M1``, sans trou, y compris après un rejeu partiel."
msgstr ""
"``nextMatchID()`` returns ``\"M\" + (nextID+1)``. Since ``nextID`` is "
"only incremented by ``match_started``, identifiers are consecutive "
"starting from ``M1``, with no gaps, including after a partial replay."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:411
msgid "``result`` et ``result_corrected``"
msgstr "``result`` and ``result_corrected``"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:429
msgid ""
"``aliveInSwiss`` relève les joueurs en vie de chaque phase "
"``swiss_lives``. ``noteRevived`` compare avant et après : un joueur que "
"la correction rend à la vie entre dans ``State.Revived``, un joueur "
"qu'elle élimine en sort ; les avertissements sont recalculés (voir "
":ref:`etat`, « Contrôle de cohérence »). ``match_started`` retire ses "
"deux joueurs de ``Revived``."
msgstr ""
"``aliveInSwiss`` collects the players still alive in each ``swiss_lives``"
" phase. ``noteRevived`` compares before and after: a player whom the "
"correction brings back to life enters ``State.Revived``, a player whom it"
" eliminates leaves it; warnings are recomputed (see :ref:`etat`, "
"\"Consistency check\"). ``match_started`` removes its two players from "
"``Revived``."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:434
msgid ""
"Une correction sur un match **annulé** le ramène à l'état ``Finished`` : "
"c'est le moyen de revenir sur une annulation."
msgstr ""
"A correction on a **cancelled** match brings it back to the ``Finished`` "
"state: this is the way to reverse a cancellation."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:437
msgid ""
"Noter que ``result_corrected`` sur un match jamais terminé fonctionne "
"aussi : il vaut alors saisie initiale suivie d'un recalcul complet (plus "
"coûteux, mais correct)."
msgstr ""
"Note that ``result_corrected`` on a match that was never finished also "
"works: it then amounts to an initial entry followed by a full "
"recomputation (more costly, but correct)."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:449
msgid ""
"Le match reste dans ``MatchOrder`` et dans ``Matches`` : le journal ne "
"perd rien. Il est simplement ignoré par tous les calculs (comptabilité, "
"adversaires rencontrés, graphes)."
msgstr ""
"The match stays in ``MatchOrder`` and in ``Matches``: the journal loses "
"nothing. It is simply ignored by all computations (accounting, opponents "
"met, graphs)."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:463
msgid ""
"Un bye ne compte ni victoire ni défaite. Il **appartient à sa ronde** : "
"le confirmer seul ne clôt pas la ronde, ses matchs restent proposés. Il "
"est mémorisé pour éviter d'en donner deux au même joueur (voir "
":ref:`format_suisse`)."
msgstr ""
"A bye counts neither as a win nor as a loss. It **belongs to its round**:"
" confirming it alone does not close the round, whose matches remain "
"proposed. It is remembered to avoid giving two to the same player (see "
":ref:`format_suisse`)."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:476
msgid "``applyDraw`` dispatche selon le format (voir :ref:`formats`) :"
msgstr "``applyDraw`` dispatches according to the format (see :ref:`formats`):"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:479
msgid "Traitement"
msgstr "Processing"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:481
msgid "``bracket``, ``lives_bracket``"
msgstr "``bracket``, ``lives_bracket``"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:481
msgid ""
"vérifie que ``len(Slots)`` est une puissance de 2 ≥ 2, puis "
"``buildBracket``"
msgstr "checks that ``len(Slots)`` is a power of 2 ≥ 2, then ``buildBracket``"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:484
msgid "``gsl``"
msgstr "``gsl``"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:484
msgid "``applyGSLDraw`` : nouveau bloc de groupes"
msgstr "``applyGSLDraw``: new block of groups"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:486
msgid "``round_robin``"
msgstr "``round_robin``"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:486
msgid ""
"``applyRRDraw`` : poules ``poule:A``, ``poule:B``… à partir de ``Groups``"
" (``Section`` vide), ou barrage (``Section =`` ``\"barrage:<lettre>\"``, "
"un seul groupe dans ``Groups``, poule ``poule:<lettre>`` existante)"
msgstr ""
"``applyRRDraw``: pools ``poule:A``, ``poule:B``… from ``Groups`` (empty "
"``Section``), or play-off (``Section =`` ``\"barrage:<lettre>\"``, a "
"single group in ``Groups``, existing pool ``poule:<lettre>``)"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:491
msgid "autre"
msgstr "other"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:491
msgid "erreur « la phase n'a pas de tirage »"
msgstr "error \"the phase has no draw\""

#: ../../source/journal.rst:522
msgid ""
"B n'est pas forcément le joueur proposé : le TD peut choisir un autre "
"joueur non qualifié de la poule (entre ex æquo, typiquement). Sans "
"``repechage`` confirmé, la place du retiré devient une exemption du "
"tableau suivant ; un journal sans ``repechage`` se rejoue donc à "
"l'identique."
msgstr ""
"B is not necessarily the proposed player: the TD may choose another non-"
"qualified player of the pool (among the tied players, typically). Without"
" a confirmed ``repechage``, the withdrawn player's slot becomes a bye in "
"the next bracket; a journal without ``repechage`` therefore replays "
"identically."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:534
msgid ""
"Change la longueur des **matchs futurs** de la phase. Les matchs déjà "
"lancés gardent leur longueur ; les ``GMatch`` déjà construits (tableau "
"tiré) gardent la leur aussi, puisqu'elle a été figée à la construction du"
" graphe. Le champ n'a donc d'effet immédiat que sur les formats à "
"appariement dynamique (suisse, barrages) et sur les graphes construits "
"**après** le changement (blocs GSL suivants). ``config_changed`` peut "
"aussi changer une longueur ; ``length_changed`` reste lu pour les "
"journaux existants."
msgstr ""
"Changes the length of the phase's **future matches**. Matches already "
"started keep their length; the ``GMatch`` already built (bracket drawn) "
"keep theirs too, since it was frozen when the graph was built. The field "
"therefore has an immediate effect only on formats with dynamic pairing "
"(Swiss, play-offs) and on graphs built **after** the change (following "
"GSL blocks). ``config_changed`` can also change a length; "
"``length_changed`` is still read for existing journals."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:551
msgid ""
"L'événement porte la configuration **entière**, et non le champ à changer"
" : ce qui est écrit dans le journal est le résultat, pas l'instruction "
"qui y mène — le même choix que pour ``draw``. Un journal se relit alors "
"sans connaître la règle de composition des retouches successives."
msgstr ""
"The event carries the **entire** configuration, not the field to change: "
"what is written in the journal is the result, not the instruction leading"
" to it — the same choice as for ``draw``. A journal can then be read back"
" without knowing the rule for composing successive adjustments."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:555
msgid "``acceptConfig`` refuse trois choses, et seulement trois :"
msgstr "``acceptConfig`` refuses three things, and only three:"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:557
msgid ""
"une configuration qui a **moins de phases** que le tournoi n'en a "
"ouvertes (une phase ouverte ne se retire pas) ;"
msgstr ""
"a configuration that has **fewer phases** than the tournament has opened "
"(an open phase cannot be removed);"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:559
msgid ""
"un changement de ``Kind`` sur une phase **terminée** (indice < "
"``Current``), **tirée** ou **commencée** (raison testée dans cet ordre) ;"
msgstr ""
"a change of ``Kind`` on a phase that is **finished** (index < "
"``Current``), **drawn** or **started** (reason tested in that order);"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:561
msgid ""
"sur un tableau (``bracket``, ``lives_bracket``) **déjà tiré**, un "
"changement de l'une des options qui ne servent qu'à construire le graphe "
"au tirage : ``consolation``, ``last_chance``, ``reconciliation``, "
"``recharge``, ``seeding``. Le graphe est fait ; les changer ne pourrait "
"plus rien produire : sans ce refus, cocher la consolante d'un tableau "
"tiré serait accepté, écrit dans la configuration, et sans effet."
msgstr ""
"on a bracket (``bracket``, ``lives_bracket``) that is **already drawn**, "
"a change to any of the options used only to build the graph at the draw: "
"``consolation``, ``last_chance``, ``reconciliation``, ``recharge``, "
"``seeding``. The graph is built; changing them could no longer produce "
"anything: without this refusal, ticking the consolation of a drawn "
"bracket would be accepted, written to the configuration, and have no "
"effect."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:567
msgid ""
"Le refus est un ``*ConfigRefusal``, qui nomme la phase, le champ et la "
"raison par des codes :"
msgstr ""
"The refusal is a ``*ConfigRefusal``, which names the phase, the field and"
" the reason by codes:"

#: ../../source/journal.rst:582
msgid ""
"``Error()`` en donne le rendu français (console, démo) ; un hôte "
"multilingue traduit les codes."
msgstr ""
"``Error()`` gives its French rendering (console, demo); a multilingual "
"host translates the codes."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:584
msgid ""
"**Journaux anciens.** Le troisième refus n'existe qu'à partir de la "
"**version 2** du journal. Un ``config_changed`` de version 0 ou 1 qui "
"changeait ces options après le tirage a été joué ainsi — accepté, sans "
"effet — et se rejoue ainsi : ``acceptConfig`` reçoit la version de "
"l'événement et n'applique le verrou du tirage qu'à partir de 2."
msgstr ""
"**Old journals.** The third refusal exists only from **version 2** of the"
" journal. A ``config_changed`` of version 0 or 1 that changed these "
"options after the draw was played that way — accepted, without effect — "
"and replays that way: ``acceptConfig`` receives the event's version and "
"applies the draw lock only from 2 on."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:593
msgid ""
"``CheckConfig`` est la **prévisualisation** : ``Validate`` puis "
"``acceptConfig`` sur une copie, aux règles de la version courante, sans "
"rien appliquer. C'est ce qu'un formulaire de réglages appelle pour griser"
" ou expliquer un champ avant d'écrire l'événement."
msgstr ""
"``CheckConfig`` is the **preview**: ``Validate`` then ``acceptConfig`` on"
" a copy, under the rules of the current version, applying nothing. This "
"is what a settings form calls to grey out or explain a field before "
"writing the event."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:597
msgid ""
"Tout le reste est accepté, y compris ce que le moteur ne peut pas juger :"
" la bascule (``target``), les longueurs à venir, les tables, les pauses, "
"la dotation, et une phase **ajoutée après** la phase courante."
msgstr ""
"Everything else is accepted, including what the engine cannot judge: the "
"switch-over (``target``), future lengths, tables, breaks, the prize "
"distribution, and a phase **added after** the current phase."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:601
msgid ""
"``setConfig`` répercute la nouvelle configuration sur les ``PhaseState`` "
"déjà ouverts. La longueur courante d'une phase (``PhaseState.Length``) ne"
" suit la configuration que si la configuration l'a **effectivement "
"changée** : sinon, une retouche qui ne touche qu'à la bascule effacerait "
"le ``length_changed`` que le TD venait de saisir à la main. Quand le "
"``Kind`` d'une phase non commencée change, sa longueur courante reprend "
"celle de la configuration et les vies de ses entrants sont recalculées "
"(``livesFor`` : ``Lives`` pour un suisse, 2 pour un GSL, 1 sinon)."
msgstr ""
"``setConfig`` propagates the new configuration to the ``PhaseState`` "
"already open. A phase's current length (``PhaseState.Length``) follows "
"the configuration only if the configuration **actually changed it**: "
"otherwise, an adjustment touching only the switch-over would erase the "
"``length_changed`` that the TD had just entered by hand. When the "
"``Kind`` of a phase that has not started changes, its current length "
"takes that of the configuration and its entrants' lives are recomputed "
"(``livesFor``: ``Lives`` for a Swiss, 2 for a GSL, 1 otherwise)."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:616
msgid ""
"Rouvre un tournoi clos, parce qu'un résultat était faux. Le classement "
"final figé est effacé et sera recalculé à la clôture suivante ; le "
"journal, lui, garde tout — la clôture, la réouverture, la correction et "
"la nouvelle clôture sont quatre événements."
msgstr ""
"Reopens a closed tournament, because a result was wrong. The frozen final"
" standings are erased and will be recomputed at the next closing; the "
"journal, for its part, keeps everything — the closing, the reopening, the"
" correction and the new closing are four events."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:629
msgid ""
"Le déplacement est **toujours accepté**, y compris vers une table qui "
"porte déjà un match en cours : le moteur avertit, il ne bloque pas. "
"``check`` lève alors ``table_shared`` (voir :ref:`etat`), qui tombe de "
"lui-même dès que l'un des deux matchs se termine ou repart ailleurs. "
"Refuser aurait laissé le TD sans recours dans la salle pleine où il en a "
"justement besoin — un plateau cassé, quatorze tables sur quatorze "
"occupées, deux joueurs qui finissent sur un coin de table en attendant."
msgstr ""
"The move is **always accepted**, including to a table that already has a "
"match in progress: the engine warns, it does not block. ``check`` then "
"raises ``table_shared`` (see :ref:`etat`), which goes away by itself as "
"soon as one of the two matches ends or moves elsewhere. Refusing would "
"have left the TD without recourse in the full playing hall where they "
"need it most — a broken board, fourteen tables out of fourteen occupied, "
"two players finishing on the corner of a table while they wait."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:643
msgid ""
"Le classement est **figé** dans ``Final``. ``StandingsCSV`` et les "
"fonctions de rendu utilisent ``Final`` s'il existe, sinon recalculent "
"``Ranking()``."
msgstr ""
"The standings are **frozen** in ``Final``. ``StandingsCSV`` and the "
"rendering functions use ``Final`` if it exists, otherwise they recompute "
"``Ranking()``."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:649
msgid ""
"Sans effet, sinon l'incrément de ``NEvents`` (ce qui décale le générateur"
" aléatoire — une note change donc le prochain tirage : c'est sans "
"conséquence sur la validité, mais à savoir)."
msgstr ""
"No effect, other than the increment of ``NEvents`` (which shifts the "
"random generator — a note therefore changes the next draw: this has no "
"consequence for validity, but is worth knowing)."

#: ../../source/journal.rst:653
